[{"id":2812745455,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6npxbv","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thanks!\r\n\r\n> @dsnopek also suggested adding the `startup` and `shutdown` callbacks while we're at it, and I may have misunderstood what he meant\r\n\r\nWhat you have is very close to what I had in mind!\r\n\r\nA common complaint is not having a spot to initialize things, since many parts of Godot aren't ready during _any_ of the initialization levels. For a portion of the folks who want singletons to be available earlier, this is what they actually want (although, not all, because some things can only be done super early). Modules can work around this problem by cheating a bit in ways that GDExtensions cannot.\r\n\r\nAnyway, the idea is to have a startup function that runs as late as possible (so, after everything within Godot has done it's thing) and a shutdown function that runs as early as possible (before anything else has started shutting down yet).\r\n\r\nThe only thing in this PR that I have notes about is the order of where these callbacks run relative to everything else.\r\n\r\nHowever, t